-- Codex Insurance Limited -- accident & sickness hospitalization policy
--
-- This file encodes ONLY the rules of the contract (fixtures/chubb-policy.txt).
-- It contains no claim data -- see apply.l4 for the nine queries and their facts.
--
-- Simplification adopted throughout (per the encoding brief): every date/time
-- fact about a claim, other than the claimant's age, is expressed as a NUMBER
-- of months elapsed since the policy's effective date. No DATE/DATETIME value
-- or arithmetic is needed anywhere in this file, and there is never a need to
-- compute the time elapsed between two dates -- every deadline below is just a
-- comparison between two such NUMBERs.
--
-- Also per the encoding brief: the agreement is assumed already signed and the
-- premium already paid, on time (Sections 1.1(1)-(2) and 3.5), so no fields or
-- rules are needed for those conditions.

§ `The insured claim`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- Section 1.1: the benefit is premised on "the hospitalization for sickness
    -- or accidental injury". Always true of a genuine claim; kept as an explicit
    -- field for faithfulness to the threshold condition in the source text.
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`                    IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Section 2.1(5): the claimant's age at the time of the hospitalization.
    -- This is the one figure the encoding brief does NOT put on the
    -- effective-date clock.
    `age at hospitalization`                                                  IS A NUMBER

    -- Section 2.1(1)-(4): what the sickness or accidental injury arose out of,
    -- directly or indirectly. These are modelled as facts about the CAUSE of
    -- the event, not as facts about the claimant's occupation or status: the
    -- policy excludes an event that arises out of one of these activities, not
    -- every event that merely happens to someone who does one of these things.
    `hospitalization arose out of skydiving`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of military service`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of fire fighter service`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of police service`                            IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Section 1.2: fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding of
    -- information provided to the Company in connection with the policy.
    `committed fraud misrepresentation or material withholding`              IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Section 1.3: the wellness-visit condition, given relative to the
    -- effective date, in months. NOTHING means the event in question has not
    -- (yet, or ever) occurred.
    `months after the effective date that the wellness visit occurred`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `months after the effective date that wellness visit confirmation was given`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER

    -- Section 1.1: the policy is only in effect "at the time of the
    -- hospitalization" -- so that is the clock every deadline above is read
    -- against, again relative to the effective date, in months.
    `months after the effective date of the hospitalization`                 IS A NUMBER


§ `1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

`wellness visit deadline in months` MEANS 6

`wellness confirmation deadline in months` MEANS 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wellness visit occurred in time` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `months after the effective date that the wellness visit occurred`
    WHEN JUST v THEN v AT MOST `wellness visit deadline in months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1.3 is pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `months after the effective date that wellness visit confirmation was given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        -- no confirmation yet: the condition is still pending, so long as the
        -- 7-month deadline has not already passed as of the hospitalization
        claim's `months after the effective date of the hospitalization` AT MOST `wellness confirmation deadline in months`
    WHEN JUST c THEN
        c AT MOST `wellness confirmation deadline in months`
        AND `the wellness visit occurred in time` claim


§ `1.1 / 1.2 -- policy in effect and cancelation`

-- Section 3.6: the policy term is one year (12 months) from the effective date.
`policy term in months` MEANS 12

-- Section 1.2: cancelation is deemed to have occurred on any of these grounds.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy has been canceled` IF
    claim's `committed fraud misrepresentation or material withholding`
    OR NOT `condition 1.3 is pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    OR claim's `months after the effective date of the hospitalization` GREATER THAN `policy term in months`

-- Section 1.1: the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization if it
-- is signed and paid up (assumed, per the encoding brief), the wellness-visit
-- condition is pending or satisfied, and it has not been canceled.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` IF
    NOT `the policy has been canceled` claim


§ `2.1 -- general exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excluded cause applies` IF
    claim's `hospitalization arose out of skydiving`
    OR claim's `hospitalization arose out of military service`
    OR claim's `hospitalization arose out of fire fighter service`
    OR claim's `hospitalization arose out of police service`
    OR claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80


§ `3.1 -- territorial scope`

-- Section 3.1.1: the policy insures the claimant twenty-four hours a day,
-- anywhere in the world. There is accordingly no geographic condition to
-- encode: travelling abroad, for instance, does not narrow coverage.


§ `3.2-3.5 -- dispute resolution, governing law, currency, premium`

-- Sections 3.2 (arbitration), 3.3 (governing law), 3.4 (currency of payment)
-- and 3.5 (timing of premium payment, assumed satisfied per the encoding
-- brief) govern how disputes are resolved and how payment is made. None of
-- them bears on whether a given hospitalization is a covered event, so none
-- of them is represented as a rule feeding into `covered` below.


§ `Coverage`

-- Section 1.1: payment of a benefit is conditioned on the hospitalization
-- being for sickness or accidental injury, on the policy being in effect at
-- the time of the hospitalization, and (Section 2.1) on no excluded cause
-- applying.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered IF
    claim's `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`
    AND `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT `an excluded cause applies` claim
